abstract: "An LLM pipeline that annotates humorous short stories using the General Theory of Verbal Humor (Attardo & Raskin, 1994). It locates each humorous instance in a text and identifies the Knowledge Resources (Script Opposition, Situation, Target, Narrative Strategy, Language) that make it funny."
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-07-07"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/iamahmadyasin/gtvh-analyzer"
url: "https://github.com/iamahmadyasin/gtvh-analyzer"
keywords:
  - computational humor
  - linguistics of humor
  - gtvh
  - nlp
  - llm
